 "paragraph": "Second disease. In the Perez et al. lupus PBMC cohort (CELLxGENE dataset 218acb0f; 162 SLE and 99 control donors; 88 libraries in 24 multiplexed pools), analysed under a plan hashed before any expression was read, pseudobulk co-expression again made false calls under a donor-centred null (20 reassignments, 99,681 pairs): 16,631 per run in classical monocytes (1,005 cells per donor, per-pair type-I 0.29) and 3,472 in plasmacytoid dendritic cells (15 cells per donor, 0.17). XDS-M made 0.0 and 0.1 (type-I 0.051, 0.050) and met the frozen rule in both; the predicted ordering by cell number did not hold. For SLE-versus-control differential co-expression, pseudobulk called 8,937 and 1,493 pairs per run under a label null, 22% and 12% of its real calls, and XDS-Mgu none. A library-preserving null is a different test, and XDS-M failed it (48,661 calls per run in monocytes, 13 in pDCs; pseudobulk 62,723 and 11,126), as did our library-split variant in monocytes; post hoc, conditioning on donor pool composition removed these calls in monocytes (0.5 per run) at the cost of mild per-pair inflation (0.061 to 0.080).",
